.policy "drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field" revision 1
.description "Keep secret model fields such as passwords, secret keys and API tokens out of a DRF ModelSerializer's output, or make them write-only."
.language python
.mode log
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. A ModelSerializer returns every field its Meta lets in: all of them with
// `fields = "__all__"`, every one `exclude` does not name, or the ones `fields` lists. When one of them holds a
// secret (a password or its hash, an API key, a token, a client or signing secret, a private key, an OTP seed,
// stored credentials), the serializer's output carries it (OWASP API3, "Broken Object Property Level
// Authorization"). The rule resolves the serializer's Meta.model to a model of the run in any module (lib/drf's
// drf_cls: through the project's import root and package re-exports too), reads its fields, own and inherited from
// the run's model bases (an abstract base in a third module), and reports, at the Meta value that lets the field in:
//   - `fields = "__all__"`, or an `exclude` that does not name the field: at that value, once per secret field;
//   - `fields` listing the field: at the listed string (lists joined with `+`, `Base.Meta.fields`, and a module
//     constant `fields = BUCKET_FIELDS` included; a string outside any class is reported at the Meta value);
//   - a SerializerMethodField in the output whose method returns `obj.<secret field>`: at the field.
// A field is a secret when its name says so and its class can hold one. Detection is by name, the one thing a
// secret column has in common, so the rule stays in log. Names (the whole name):
// `[*_]password[s][_hash]` (`passwd`, `passphrase`), `[*_]secret[s][_key|_access_key|_token|_value]`,
// `[*_]token[_key|_secret|_value]`, `[*_]tokens_(key|secret|value)`, `[*_](api|secret|private|signing|encryption)[_]key[s]`,
// `[*_](otp|totp|hotp)[_secret|_seed|_key]`, `[*_](mfa|2fa)_(secret|seed|key)`, `[*_]credential[s]`. The plural
// `tokens` alone (NLP tokens, stored LLM token counts) and `access_key` without `secret` (an object-storage key id,
// whose secret is `secret_access_key`) name non-secrets more often than secrets and are not on the list. Classes
// that cannot hold one are left out: booleans, numbers, dates and times, durations, auto keys, relations (a relation
// returns the related row's key). A field class the run defines (`EncryptedTextField`) or imports from another
// package counts when it is called `…Field`. A model deriving from Django's AbstractBaseUser, AbstractUser or User
// (Django's `User`, `get_user_model()`, or a module's `User = get_user_model()`) has `password`, Django's hash.
//   class ApiClient(CredentialModel): ...              # core/models.py: CredentialModel has api_token
//   class ApiClientSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
//       class Meta:
//           model = ApiClient
//           exclude = ["owner"]                        reported: api_token goes out
//   class UserCreateSerializer(serializers.ModelSerializer):
//       class Meta:
//           model = User
//           fields = ["id", "username", "password"]
//           extra_kwargs = {"password": {"write_only": True}}         not reported
// It leaves alone a field the serializer hides: declared (by the serializer or a run base it inherits the name from)
// as `x = None`, as a field with `write_only=True`, a HiddenField or SerializerMethodField, a field reading another
// `source=`, or a field class that is not rest_framework's own (a project's ObfuscatedPasswordField); with no
// declaration, `Meta.extra_kwargs` giving it `write_only: True` (lib/drf's drf_extra_kw: a literal, `dict(...)` or
// a module constant); and a serializer with a `to_representation` (its own or a run base's) whose class body, or a
// run base's, holds the field's name as a string outside its Meta (`data.pop("password")`, or a
// `secure_fields = ["password"]` list the method pops). Also left alone: secret-looking names that are not secrets
// by class or name (`password_changed_at`, `token_expires`, `has_password`, `tokens_used`, `tokens`, `access_key`, a
// BooleanField `secret_santa`), plain Serializers, serializers whose model is outside the run (other than Django's
// users), and test code.
// Gaps: a declared plain field next to `extra_kwargs` write_only is reported (DRF ignores extra_kwargs for declared
// fields, so it is exposed); a secret under a name the list misses (`key`, `pin`, `salt`) is not reported; tokens
// meant to be shown are reported, since no name separates them: a token returned once by the endpoint that creates
// it, an invite or share-link token, a device's pairing token; a serializer only ever used to validate input (never
// rendered) is reported; a plain Serializer declaring `secret_access_key = CharField()` is not; `fields` built by a
// call or a comprehension is not read; a to_representation that pops the field without naming it in the class (a
// helper in another module) is reported.

#include "lib/drf.rerail"

.violation SerializerExposesSecret(at: node, ser: symbol, model: symbol, x: symbol, how: symbol) "`{ser}` puts `{model}.{x}`, a secret, in its output ({how}). Drop it from the output or make it write-only, unless this serializer shows a token once to its creator."
SerializerExposesSecret(at, s, m, x, how) :- sx_out(c, mq, x, at, how), !sx_hidden(c, x), def_name(c, s),
    sx_model_label(mq, m).
SerializerExposesSecret(at, s, m, x, "a SerializerMethodField returns it") :- sx_method_out(c, mq, x, at),
    def_name(c, s), sx_model_label(mq, m).

// sx_model_label(mq, m): the model's name for the message: its class name, or `User` for get_user_model().
.decl sx_model_label(mq: symbol, m: symbol)
sx_model_label(mq, m) :- sx_ser(_, mq), mq != "get_user_model()", split_dot(mq, _, m).
sx_model_label("get_user_model()", "User").

// ---- names across import roots ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// sx_super(c, b): class b of the run is among class c's bases, directly or not, through lib/drf's drf_cls (the
// project's import root, package re-exports): model bases and serializer bases alike.
.decl sx_super(c: node, b: node)
sx_super(c, b) :- class_base(c, q), drf_cls(q, b).
sx_super(c, b) :- sx_super(c, m), class_base(m, q), drf_cls(q, b).

// ---- serializers and their models --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// sx_ms(c): c is a ModelSerializer: lib/drf's drf_model_serializer, or a class with one among its sx_super bases.
.decl sx_ms(c: node)
sx_ms(c) :- drf_model_serializer(c).
sx_ms(c) :- sx_super(c, b), drf_model_serializer(b).
// sx_meta_opt(c, k, v): ModelSerializer c's Meta option k is v: lib/drf's drf_meta_opt, else (a serializer lib/drf
// does not see) the option of the `class Meta` in c's own body.
.decl sx_meta_opt(c: node, k: symbol, v: node)
sx_meta_opt(c, k, v) :- sx_ms(c), drf_meta_opt(c, k, v).
sx_meta_opt(c, k, v) :- sx_ms(c), !drf_node(c), kind(m, "class_definition"), def_name(m, "Meta"), nearest(m, c, scope),
    drf_own_attr(m, k, v, _).

// sx_ser(c, mq): c is a ModelSerializer outside test code whose Meta.model is mq: a qualified class name, or
// "get_user_model()" for `model = get_user_model()`.
.decl sx_ser(c: node, mq: symbol)
sx_ser(c, mq) :- sx_meta_opt(c, "model", v), unparen(v, u), sym_of(u, mq), docof(c, d), !dj_test_doc(d).
sx_ser(c, "get_user_model()") :- sx_meta_opt(c, "model", v), unparen(v, u), sx_gum_call(u), docof(c, d),
    !dj_test_doc(d).
// `UserModel = get_user_model()` in the serializer's own module, then `model = UserModel`.
sx_ser(c, "get_user_model()") :- sx_meta_opt(c, "model", v), unparen(v, u), kind(u, "identifier"), look(u, x, s),
    asg(s, x, r, _), unparen(r, g), sx_gum_call(g), docof(c, d), !dj_test_doc(d).
.decl sx_gum_call(u: node)
sx_gum_call(u) :- kind(u, "call"), field(u, "function", f), sym_of(f, q),
    (q = "django.contrib.auth.get_user_model" ; q = "django.contrib.auth.models.get_user_model").

// sx_user(mq): Meta.model mq is a user model with Django's `password` field: Django's own user classes, a run class
// deriving from one, `get_user_model()`, or another module's `User = get_user_model()` (mq is "<module>.User").
.decl sx_user_lib(q: symbol)
sx_user_lib("django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractUser"). sx_user_lib("django.contrib.auth.models.AbstractBaseUser").
sx_user_lib("django.contrib.auth.base_user.AbstractBaseUser"). sx_user_lib("django.contrib.auth.models.User").
.decl sx_user_alias(q: symbol)
sx_user_alias(q) :- modname(m, mod), rasg(m, x, r, _), unparen(r, u), sx_gum_call(u), q = cat(mod, ".", x).
.decl sx_user(mq: symbol)
sx_user("get_user_model()") :- sx_ser(_, "get_user_model()").
sx_user(mq) :- sx_ser(_, mq), sx_user_lib(mq).
sx_user(mq) :- sx_ser(_, mq), drf_cls(mq, k), class_base(k, b), sx_user_lib(b).
sx_user(mq) :- sx_ser(_, mq), drf_cls(mq, k), sx_super(k, a), class_base(a, b), sx_user_lib(b).
sx_user(mq) :- sx_ser(_, mq), sx_user_alias(aq), (aq = mq ; suffix(cat(".", mq), aq)).

// sx_meta_mc(mc): model class mc of the run is some serializer's Meta.model: the only models whose fields are read.
.decl sx_meta_mc(mc: node)
sx_meta_mc(mc) :- sx_ser(_, mq), drf_cls(mq, mc).
// sx_body_field(c, x, t): class c's body assigns `x = <call>` with the callee's last name t ending in "Field": a model
// field class lib/django does not know too (the run's EncryptedTextField, a package's AESField).
.decl sx_body_field(c: node, x: symbol, t: symbol)
sx_body_field(c, x, t) :- drf_own_attr(c, x, v, _), unparen(v, k), kind(k, "call"), call_name(k, t), suffix("Field", t).
sx_body_field(c, x, t) :- dj_class_field(c, x, _, t).
// sx_model_field(mc, x, t): model mc has field x of class t, its own or a run base's (an abstract base, a mixin).
.decl sx_model_field(mc: node, x: symbol, t: symbol)
sx_model_field(mc, x, t) :- sx_meta_mc(mc), sx_body_field(mc, x, t).
sx_model_field(mc, x, t) :- sx_meta_mc(mc), sx_super(mc, b), sx_body_field(b, x, t).

// sx_secret(mq, x): model mq has a field x holding a secret.
.decl sx_secret(mq: symbol, x: symbol)
sx_secret(mq, x) :- sx_ser(_, mq), drf_cls(mq, mc), sx_model_field(mc, x, t), sx_secret_name(x), !sx_plain_class(t).
sx_secret(mq, "password") :- sx_user(mq).

// sx_secret_name(x): the whole name x names a secret.
.decl sx_secret_name(x: symbol)
sx_secret_name(x) :- sx_model_field(_, x, _),
    (match("(?:.*_)?(?:password|passwd|passphrase)s?(?:_hash|_hashed|_digest)?", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?secrets?(?:_key|_access_key|_token|_value)?", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?token(?:_key|_secret|_value)?", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?tokens_(?:key|secret|value)", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?(?:api|secret|private|signing|encryption)_?keys?", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?(?:otp|totp|hotp)(?:_secret|_seed|_key)?", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?(?:mfa|2fa)_(?:secret|seed|key)", x) ;
     match("(?:.*_)?credentials?", x)).
// sx_plain_class(t): model field classes that cannot hold a secret.
.decl sx_plain_class(t: symbol)
sx_plain_class(t) :- sx_model_field(_, _, t), (suffix("IntegerField", t) ; suffix("AutoField", t) ; dj_relation_class(t) ;
    t = "BooleanField" ; t = "NullBooleanField" ; t = "DateTimeField" ; t = "DateField" ; t = "TimeField" ;
    t = "DurationField" ; t = "FloatField" ; t = "DecimalField").

// ---- what goes out -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// sx_out(c, mq, x, at, how): serializer c (model mq) returns secret field x, let in by Meta value or string `at`.
.decl sx_out(c: node, mq: symbol, x: symbol, at: node, how: symbol)
sx_out(c, mq, x, v, "`fields = \"__all__\"` includes it") :- sx_ser(c, mq), sx_meta_opt(c, "fields", v), unparen(v, u),
    str(u, "__all__"), sx_secret(mq, x).
sx_out(c, mq, x, v, "`exclude` does not name it") :- sx_ser(c, mq), sx_meta_opt(c, "exclude", v), sx_secret(mq, x),
    !drf_str_elem(v, x).
sx_out(c, mq, x, at, "`fields` lists it") :- sx_ser(c, mq), sx_meta_opt(c, "fields", v), drf_str_at(v, e, x),
    sx_secret(mq, x), sx_at(v, e, at).
// sx_at(v, e, at): report a listed name at its string when it is written in a class (the Meta, or a base's Meta),
// else (a module constant) at the Meta value v.
.decl sx_at(v: node, e: node, at: node)
sx_at(v, e, e) :- sx_fields_val(v), drf_str_at(v, e, _), nearest(e, _, "class_definition").
sx_at(v, e, v) :- sx_fields_val(v), drf_str_at(v, e, _), !nearest(e, _, "class_definition").
.decl sx_fields_val(v: node)
sx_fields_val(v) :- sx_meta_opt(c, "fields", v), sx_ser(c, _).

// sx_method_out(c, mq, x, at): serializer c (model mq) declares SerializerMethodField `at` in its output (`fields`
// lists it, or is "__all__", or Meta uses `exclude`), whose method (`get_<name>`, or `method_name=`) returns
// `<obj>.x`, obj its instance parameter and x a secret field of mq.
.decl sx_method_out(c: node, mq: symbol, x: symbol, at: node)
sx_method_out(c, mq, x, k) :- sx_ser(c, mq), drf_declared(c, f, k), drf_field_kind(k, "SerializerMethodField"),
    sx_in_output(c, f), sx_method_name(k, f, mn), drf_method(c, mn, fn), params(fn, o, 1), kind(r, "return_statement"),
    def_frame(r, fn), child(r, e, 0), unparen(e, a), attr_of(a, on, x), kind(on, "identifier"), text(on, o),
    sx_secret(mq, x).
.decl sx_method_name(k: node, f: symbol, mn: symbol)
sx_method_name(k, f, mn) :- drf_field_kind(k, "SerializerMethodField"), drf_declared(_, f, k), drf_kw(k, "method_name", v),
    str(v, mn).
sx_method_name(k, f, mn) :- drf_field_kind(k, "SerializerMethodField"), drf_declared(_, f, k),
    !drf_kw(k, "method_name", _), mn = cat("get_", f).
.decl sx_in_output(c: node, f: symbol)
sx_in_output(c, f) :- sx_ser(c, _), drf_declared(c, f, _), sx_meta_opt(c, "fields", v), drf_str_elem(v, f).
sx_in_output(c, f) :- sx_ser(c, _), drf_declared(c, f, _), sx_meta_opt(c, "fields", v), unparen(v, u), str(u, "__all__").
sx_in_output(c, f) :- sx_ser(c, _), drf_declared(c, f, _), sx_meta_opt(c, "exclude", v), !drf_str_elem(v, f).

// ---- what hides it -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.decl sx_hidden(c: node, x: symbol)
// A declaration of x replaces the model field: hidden unless it is rest_framework's own field reading x for output.
sx_hidden(c, x) :- sx_out(c, _, x, _, _), sx_decl_value(c, x, _), !sx_decl_exposes(c, x).
sx_hidden(c, x) :- sx_out(c, _, x, _, _), drf_extra_kw(c, x, "write_only", t), kind(t, "true"), !sx_declares(c, x).
// A to_representation (own or a run base's) next to the name as a string in the class body or a run base's, outside
// a Meta: `data.pop("password")`, or a `secure_fields = ["password"]` list the method pops in a loop.
sx_hidden(c, x) :- sx_out(c, _, x, _, _), sx_to_rep(c), sx_names_in_body(c, c, x).
sx_hidden(c, x) :- sx_out(c, _, x, _, _), sx_to_rep(c), sx_super(c, b), sx_names_in_body(c, b, x).
.decl sx_to_rep(c: node)
sx_to_rep(c) :- sx_ser(c, _), drf_own_method(c, "to_representation", _).
sx_to_rep(c) :- sx_ser(c, _), sx_super(c, b), drf_own_method(b, "to_representation", _).
.decl sx_names_in_body(c: node, k: node, x: symbol)
sx_names_in_body(c, k, x) :- sx_out(c, _, x, _, _), str(n, x), nearest(n, k, "class_definition").

// sx_decl_value(c, x, u): serializer c's attribute x is u: its own `x = u`, else a run ancestor's.
.decl sx_decl_value(c: node, x: symbol, u: node)
sx_decl_value(c, x, u) :- sx_out(c, _, x, _, _), drf_own_attr(c, x, v, _), unparen(v, u).
sx_decl_value(c, x, u) :- sx_out(c, _, x, _, _), sx_super(c, b), drf_own_attr(b, x, v, _), !drf_own_attr_name(c, x),
    unparen(v, u).
.decl sx_declares(c: node, x: symbol)
sx_declares(c, x) :- sx_decl_value(c, x, _).
// sx_decl_exposes(c, x): the declaration is a rest_framework field, not HiddenField or SerializerMethodField, without
// write_only=True and without a `source=` naming another attribute.
.decl sx_decl_exposes(c: node, x: symbol)
sx_decl_exposes(c, x) :- sx_decl_value(c, x, u), kind(u, "call"), field(u, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q),
    prefix("rest_framework.", q), split_dot(q, _, n), n != "HiddenField", n != "SerializerMethodField",
    !drf_kw_true(u, "write_only"), !sx_other_source(u, x).
.decl sx_other_source(u: node, x: symbol)
sx_other_source(u, x) :- sx_decl_value(_, x, u), drf_kw(u, "source", sv), !str(sv, x).

// The cases, `cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/`, read as one repository: each line ending in
// `# caught` is reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "core/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/core/__init__.py"
    .fixture "core/fields.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/core/fields.py"
    .fixture "core/models.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/core/models.py"
    .fixture "accounts/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/accounts/__init__.py"
    .fixture "accounts/models.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/accounts/models.py"
    .fixture "accounts/serializers.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/accounts/serializers.py"
    .fixture "accounts/tests/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/accounts/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "accounts/tests/test_serializers.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/accounts/tests/test_serializers.py"
    .fixture "integrations/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/integrations/__init__.py"
    .fixture "integrations/models.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/integrations/models.py"
    .fixture "integrations/serializers.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/integrations/serializers.py"
    .fixture "backend/vault/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/backend/vault/__init__.py"
    .fixture "backend/vault/models.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/backend/vault/models.py"
    .fixture "backend/vault/api/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/backend/vault/api/__init__.py"
    .fixture "backend/vault/api/base.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/backend/vault/api/base.py"
    .fixture "backend/vault/api/serializers.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/backend/vault/api/serializers.py"
    .fixture "storage/__init__.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/storage/__init__.py"
    .fixture "storage/constants.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/storage/constants.py"
    .fixture "storage/models.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/storage/models.py"
    .fixture "storage/serializers.py" from "../cases/drf-practice-serializer-exposes-secret-field/storage/serializers.py"
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":15
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":22
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":32
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":40
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":47
    .expect _ at "accounts/serializers.py":56
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":14
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":22
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":23
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":31
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":39
    .expect _ at "integrations/serializers.py":106
    .expect _ at "backend/vault/api/serializers.py":9
    .expect _ at "backend/vault/api/serializers.py":25
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":16
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":23
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":30
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":35
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":47
    .expect _ at "storage/serializers.py":61
.end
